UI-Mate adapter provenance
==========================

This adapter directly vendors Tencent's official UI-Mate prompt construction,
history collapsing, XML response parser, coordinate scaling, pyautogui action
translation, and optional demonstration workflow from:

  https://github.com/Tencent/UI-Mate
  commit d185dc9d74cfcab3a890d7ffb2bb011ecdd64c64
  source archive SHA-256 12046e80b390539417bfc803d1effcd7b867a4bb95ac8a20a5631ce60db9ab4d

The following files are byte-identical to that commit:

  agents/__init__.py
    SHA-256 e7cd2a9ff9e93cde70d9c0cbe6d475a9707cf6c9849effb27285739b6cb77c46
  agents/ui_mate_agent.py
    SHA-256 60e1f6924745333dcb0d363e7187d9045d04c06924a1150f02d334311fc38d77
  agents/demo_workflow.py
    SHA-256 4939d179bc15035661819efa149c3e1a7a5075a2f2334478e3c53e49991fd0a4

The upstream change since the prior pin only publishes OSWorkerBench and edits
README links; these vendored serving-harness files remain byte-identical.

LICENSE.upstream is Tencent's repository license text. The Vonk wrapper only
starts vLLM and exposes a non-actuating one-step client; it does not alter the
official prompt or parser. Predicted pyautogui strings are returned to the
caller and are never executed inside the model container.
